# Multi-state variable — refused (PHASE5C-TUTORIAL §3, the 2-4 flank)

The tutorial's 2-4 shape also carries multi-`state` variables. Catala expands
each state into a separate scopelang variable; the IR has no state machinery.
Refused loudly (a `#`-suffixed scopelang variable name is the tell).

```catala
declaration scope Aanslag:
  input grondslag content integer
  output heffing content integer
    state basis
    state gecorrigeerd

scope Aanslag:
  definition heffing state basis equals grondslag
  definition heffing state gecorrigeerd equals heffing - 10
```
